 "dump_paths_note": "The dump directories are transient trust-side scratch. What pins each measurement is `dump_sha256` over the artifact bytes and the binary-format version, both recorded above; the paths are provenance, not an interface.",
 "reproduce": "cargo build --release --manifest-path scripts/crystal_a2_project/Cargo.toml && ./target/release/a2project <crate.trust-ir.bin> <fn-name> <out-dir> [slug]",
 "func_namespace_note": "`crate_func_ids_seen` is the ONE namespace the core module's `(func N ...)` and `(call M ...)` share, in canonical order. Its head is always the body's OWN id -- that is what `self interned first` means on reader A's side, and `crystal_a2_mint`'s M8 lane asserts `crate_func_ids_seen[i][0] == artifact_func_id[i]` for every producer of every row. Ten of the eleven bodies call nothing, so their lists are exactly that one entry. `level_is_zero` is the only body that calls anything: it calls `<LevelArc as Deref>::deref` three times and ITSELF three times, which is why it is the one row where the collision was observable and the one chain whose tag table carries a non-empty `funcs` lane. The IDS move across the three dumps and the NAMES do not, which is why both are recorded and why a reviewer checks the name."
}
